From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: only drop the waited fence of the context destroyed

When a context is destroyed while the sync thread waits on a fence,
vrend_free_fences_for_context cleared fence_waiting->ctx without checking
that the fence belongs to that context. A fence of another context (or a
ctx0 fence, which every virgl GL guest uses) then never reported its
retire. The guest only got it with the next fence, or never if nothing
else was submitted.

Upstream: yes, a plain bug in virglrenderer (any platform with
VIRGL_RENDERER_THREAD_SYNC). Not sent.
Test: glmark2 loops of short runs (a GL context created and destroyed
every few seconds) in an app VM with async fences.

--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -7362,7 +7362,7 @@
          if (fence->ctx == ctx)
             free_fence_locked(fence);
       }
-      if (vrend_state.fence_waiting) {
+      if (vrend_state.fence_waiting && vrend_state.fence_waiting->ctx == ctx) {
          /* mark the fence invalid as the sync thread is still waiting on it */
          vrend_state.fence_waiting->ctx = NULL;
       }
